@lang en
IMPORT `baominh-par-exclusions`

-- Fixtures for the tests modules: named scenario values and the builders that make them.
-- No directives here. EVERY FIGURE IN THIS FILE IS A SCENARIO VALUE chosen by the encoder to make
-- the arithmetic visible (a sum insured of 1,000,000,000 VND, a deductible of 10,000,000 VND,
-- and so on); the document states no amount, and none of these is the document's.

§ `Fixtures`

§§ `The Schedule`

GIVEN d IS A STRING
      n IS A NUMBER
      p IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An item in the Schedule`
`a scheduled item` d `insured for` n `with paid already` p MEANS
    `An item in the Schedule` WITH
        `description`                                          IS d
        `sum insured`                                          IS n
        `already paid on this item in the period of insurance` IS p

`the building` MEANS `a scheduled item` "factory building" `insured for` 1000000000 `with paid already` 0
`the stock`    MEANS `a scheduled item` "stock in trade"   `insured for`  500000000 `with paid already` 0

`the year 2026` MEANS `A period` WITH `first day` IS YMD 2026 1 1
                                    , `last day`  IS YMD 2026 12 31

GIVEN `the deductible`  IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the limits`      IS A LIST OF `A limit of liability`
      `the renewals`    IS A LIST OF `A period`
      `paid or agreed`  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The Schedule`
`a Schedule for 2026 with` `the deductible` `the limits` `the renewals` `paid or agreed` MEANS
    `The Schedule` WITH
        `policy number`                                     IS "TEST-1"
        `the period of insurance`                           IS `the year 2026`
        `renewal periods paid for and accepted`             IS `the renewals`
        `the items`                                         IS LIST `the building`, `the stock`
        `the total sum insured`                             IS 1500000000
        `already paid under this policy in the period`      IS 0
        `the limits of liability`                           IS `the limits`
        `the deductible for each loss`                      IS `the deductible`
        `the annual premium`                                IS 12000000
        `the premium for the period`                        IS 12000000
        `the Insured has paid or agreed to pay the premium` IS `paid or agreed`

-- The ordinary Schedule: a deductible of 10,000,000 for each loss, no limits, no renewal.
`the Schedule` MEANS `a Schedule for 2026 with` (JUST 10000000) EMPTY EMPTY TRUE
`the Schedule without a deductible` MEANS `a Schedule for 2026 with` NOTHING EMPTY EMPTY TRUE

§§ `Links in a chain of causation`

GIVEN c IS A `A cause`
GIVETH A `A link in the chain of causation`
`directly` c MEANS `A link in the chain of causation` WITH
    `the cause` IS c, `direct` IS TRUE, `resulting from earlier Damage by` IS NOTHING

GIVEN c IS A `A cause`
GIVETH A `A link in the chain of causation`
`indirectly` c MEANS `A link in the chain of causation` WITH
    `the cause` IS c, `direct` IS FALSE, `resulting from earlier Damage by` IS NOTHING

GIVEN c IS A `A cause`
      e IS A `A cause`
GIVETH A `A link in the chain of causation`
`directly` c `, after earlier Damage by` e MEANS `A link in the chain of causation` WITH
    `the cause` IS c, `direct` IS TRUE, `resulting from earlier Damage by` IS JUST e

GIVEN c IS A `A cause`
      e IS A `A cause`
GIVETH A `A link in the chain of causation`
`indirectly` c `, after earlier Damage by` e MEANS `A link in the chain of causation` WITH
    `the cause` IS c, `direct` IS FALSE, `resulting from earlier Damage by` IS JUST e

§§ `The circumstances of an item`

-- A checklist, so that a test names only what differs from the ordinary case: an item at the
-- insured premises with nothing else true.
DECLARE `A circumstance` IS ONE OF
    `away from the insured premises`
    `movable`
    `in the open`
    `stated as insured`
    `in transit`
    `under construction`
    `being installed or moved`
    `under repair`
    `insured some other way`
    `marine`

GIVEN fs IS A LIST OF `A circumstance`
GIVETH A `The circumstances of the item`
`circumstances with` fs MEANS `The circumstances of the item` WITH
    `at the insured premises`                                        IS NOT elem `away from the insured premises` fs
    `movable`                                                        IS elem `movable` fs
    `in the open or in a building without walls`                     IS elem `in the open` fs
    `stated as insured in this policy`                               IS elem `stated as insured` fs
    `in transit outside the insured premises`                        IS elem `in transit` fs
    `in the course of demolition, construction or erection, or materials supplied for it` IS elem `under construction` fs
    `being installed or moved`                                       IS elem `being installed or moved` fs
    `undergoing repair, inspection, installation or maintenance`     IS elem `under repair` fs
    `insured in some other way`                                      IS elem `insured some other way` fs
    `insured, or such that it would have to be insured, under a marine policy` IS elem `marine` fs

`the ordinary circumstances` MEANS `circumstances with` EMPTY

§§ `Valuations`

GIVEN `the Damage`       IS A NUMBER
      `the actual value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The valuation of the item`
`Damage of` `the Damage` `to property worth` `the actual value` MEANS `The valuation of the item` WITH
    `the Damage, valued at the time of the loss`                      IS `the Damage`
    `the part of the Damage arising from a cause not excluded`        IS NOTHING
    `the actual value of the item at the time of the loss`            IS JUST `the actual value`
    `sums insured by other insurances of the same property or loss`   IS EMPTY
    `the amount the marine policy would pay if this policy did not exist` IS NOTHING
    `the costs of the media`                                          IS NOTHING

GIVEN `the Damage`       IS A NUMBER
      `the part`         IS A NUMBER
      `the actual value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The valuation of the item`
`Damage of` `the Damage` `, of which not excluded` `the part` `, to property worth` `the actual value` MEANS `The valuation of the item` WITH
    `the Damage, valued at the time of the loss`                      IS `the Damage`
    `the part of the Damage arising from a cause not excluded`        IS JUST `the part`
    `the actual value of the item at the time of the loss`            IS JUST `the actual value`
    `sums insured by other insurances of the same property or loss`   IS EMPTY
    `the amount the marine policy would pay if this policy did not exist` IS NOTHING
    `the costs of the media`                                          IS NOTHING

-- The ordinary valuation for the cover and exclusions tests: 100,000,000 of Damage to property
-- worth 1,000,000,000 (its full sum insured, so no average).
`the ordinary valuation` MEANS `Damage of` 100000000 `to property worth` 1000000000

§§ `What the Insured said`

`nothing false was said` MEANS `What the Insured told the Insurer about the item` WITH
    `false information about the property, the building, the business or the premises` IS FALSE
    `a misstatement of a material fact`                                     IS FALSE
    `an omission of a fact on which the Insurer assessed the risk`          IS FALSE

§§ `Items`

-- The general builder: the building's Schedule entry, with the kind, chain, circumstances and
-- valuation given; nothing misdescribed, no change under GC 8, not a computer-system cost.
GIVEN k  IS A `A kind of property`
      ch IS A LIST OF `A link in the chain of causation`
      c  IS A `The circumstances of the item`
      v  IS A `The valuation of the item`
GIVETH A `A damaged item`
`an item of` k `damaged by` ch `in` c `valued` v MEANS `A damaged item` WITH
    `the item insured`                  IS `the building`
    `kind`                              IS k
    `the chain of causation`            IS ch
    `circumstances`                     IS c
    `valuation`                         IS v
    `what the Insured told the Insurer` IS `nothing false was said`
    `changes under General Condition 8` IS EMPTY
    `claimed as a cost of changing or adding to a computer system, programme, software or chip` IS FALSE

-- The short builder: ordinary circumstances and the ordinary valuation.
GIVEN k  IS A `A kind of property`
      ch IS A LIST OF `A link in the chain of causation`
GIVETH A `A damaged item`
`a damaged` k `by` ch MEANS `an item of` k `damaged by` ch `in` `the ordinary circumstances` `valued` `the ordinary valuation`

-- With circumstances.
GIVEN k  IS A `A kind of property`
      ch IS A LIST OF `A link in the chain of causation`
      fs IS A LIST OF `A circumstance`
GIVETH A `A damaged item`
`a damaged` k `by` ch `where` fs MEANS `an item of` k `damaged by` ch `in` (`circumstances with` fs) `valued` `the ordinary valuation`

§§ `Conduct`

GIVEN `days to the claim` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `longer period`     IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `immediate`         IS A BOOLEAN
      `police told`       IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The claims procedure as performed`
`a claims procedure with` `days to the claim` `longer period` `immediate` `police told` MEANS
    `The claims procedure as performed` WITH
        `measures to minimise the loss were taken immediately`                       IS `immediate`
        `written notice was given to the Insurer immediately`                        IS `immediate`
        `the police were notified immediately`                                       IS `police told`
        `days from awareness to the written claim`                                   IS `days to the claim`
        `a longer period agreed in writing by the Insurer, in days`                  IS `longer period`
        `particulars of other insurances were given`                                 IS TRUE
        `the information and documents the Insurer reasonably required were provided, with a declaration of truth` IS TRUE

-- Everything done: notice and measures immediately, police told, the claim on day 10.
`the procedure followed` MEANS `a claims procedure with` (JUST 10) NOTHING TRUE TRUE

-- A checklist of departures from good conduct.
DECLARE `A lapse` IS ONE OF
    `a fraudulent claim`
    `fraudulent means`
    `refusing subrogation`
    `not complying with General Condition 10`
    `hindering the Insurer`
    `withholding reinstatement plans`
    `poor maintenance`
    `a precaution not taken`
    `insuring the deductible`

GIVEN ls IS A LIST OF `A lapse`
      cp IS A `The claims procedure as performed`
GIVETH A `The Insured's conduct`
`conduct with` ls `and` cp MEANS `The Insured's conduct` WITH
    `the claim is fraudulent in some respect`                                    IS elem `a fraudulent claim` ls
    `fraudulent means or devices were used to obtain a benefit`                  IS elem `fraudulent means` ls
    `refused an act the Insurer required to enforce its rights against others`   IS elem `refusing subrogation` ls
    `did not comply with a requirement of the Insurer under General Condition 10` IS elem `not complying with General Condition 10` ls
    `hindered the Insurer in exercising its powers under General Condition 10`   IS elem `hindering the Insurer` ls
    `did not provide the plans and information required for a reinstatement`   IS elem `withholding reinstatement plans` ls
    `maintained the property properly`                                           IS NOT elem `poor maintenance` ls
    `took every precaution to prevent loss`                                      IS NOT elem `a precaution not taken` ls
    `insured the deductible elsewhere`                                           IS elem `insuring the deductible` ls
    `the claims procedure`                                                       IS cp

`good conduct` MEANS `conduct with` EMPTY `and` `the procedure followed`

§§ `The premium`

-- Accepted on 1 January 2026, paid in full on 5 January, no instalments.
`the premium paid on time` MEANS `The premium payment` WITH
    `the Insurer accepted payment by instalments`                IS FALSE
    `date the cover was accepted`                                IS YMD 2026 1 1
    `date the premium was paid in full`                          IS JUST (YMD 2026 1 5)
    `agreed date of the first later instalment not paid on time` IS NOTHING

GIVEN `paid on` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `The premium payment`
`the premium paid on` `paid on` MEANS `The premium payment` WITH
    `the Insurer accepted payment by instalments`                IS FALSE
    `date the cover was accepted`                                IS YMD 2026 1 1
    `date the premium was paid in full`                          IS `paid on`
    `agreed date of the first later instalment not paid on time` IS NOTHING

§§ `Losses`

-- The general builder.
GIVEN d   IS A DATE
      its IS A LIST OF `A damaged item`
      th  IS A MAYBE `The circumstances of a theft`
      ac  IS A MAYBE `An act of force or violence`
      dp  IS A MAYBE `When the Damage happened, relative to a dispossession`
      em  IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      cd  IS A `The Insured's conduct`
      pr  IS A `The premium payment`
GIVETH A `A loss`
`a loss on` d `of` its `with theft` th `act` ac `dispossession` dp `building empty` em `conduct` cd `premium` pr MEANS
    `A loss` WITH
        `date of the loss`                                  IS d
        `physical loss, destruction or damage`              IS TRUE
        `sudden and unforeseen`                             IS TRUE
        `the damaged items`                                 IS its
        `the theft`                                         IS th
        `the act of force or violence`                      IS ac
        `when the Damage happened, relative to the dispossession` IS dp
        `the insured building was empty or not in use`      IS em
        `theft or a malicious act was suspected`            IS FALSE
        `the Insured's conduct`                             IS cd
        `the premium payment`                               IS pr

-- The ordinary loss: 1 June 2026, good conduct, premium paid on time, no special facts.
GIVEN items IS A LIST OF `A damaged item`
GIVETH A `A loss`
`a loss of` items MEANS
    `a loss on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `of` items `with theft` NOTHING `act` NOTHING `dispossession` NOTHING `building empty` NOTHING `conduct` `good conduct` `premium` `the premium paid on time`

-- The ordinary loss of one item.
GIVEN i IS A `A damaged item`
GIVETH A `A loss`
`a loss of the item` i MEANS `a loss of` (LIST i)
